 Each task has a list-unique string `id` (for example, `task-1`) that stays with it when renamed. The
 result from `add` includes that id. Use `get(id)` to retrieve a task by id; `find` and the task-changing
 methods (`complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove`) accept either its title or id.
+Tasks also include `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings. They match when a task is
+added; `updatedAt` changes when the task's status, title or tags change. `createTodoList` accepts an
+optional function that supplies timestamps, which is useful when the app needs a controlled clock.
 
 Run its tests with `npm test`.
