@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: task-002-record-task-creation-and-update-timestamps
+type: task
+title: "Record task creation and update timestamps"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Record when each task was created and last changed. Expose `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as
+ISO-8601 date-time strings. Set both to the same time when a task is added, and refresh
+`updatedAt` whenever a task is completed, reopened, renamed, tagged or untagged.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Added tasks expose `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, initially equal and valid ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- Successful changes to a task refresh `updatedAt` while preserving `createdAt`.
+- The app's public API lets callers provide deterministic time without domain code reading the clock.
+- README documents the timestamps.
+
+## Outcome
+
+Tasks now expose both timestamps. Creation captures one supplied ISO string for both fields, and
+successful status, title and tag changes refresh `updatedAt`. The app factory supplies the current
+ISO string by default and accepts an injected timestamp function. README documents the behavior.
